Description: device tree properties whose names have 32 to 255 characters
 xnu's flattened device tree holds property names of up to 31
 characters, so pieboot passes a property with a name of 32 to 255
 characters as pieboot,long,N, N counting from 0 in its node, whose value
 is the name, a NUL, then the property's value. MakeReferenceTable, which
 builds the device tree plane, gives such a property its name back and a
 copy of its value, so drivers find it under its own name, 4-byte aligned
 like every other value. A pieboot,long,N value whose name is shorter or
 longer, or has no NUL before its end, stays as it is. The early boot
 code, which reads the flattened tree, sees only the pieboot,long,N names.
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-19

